# Assurance policy: production template.  NOT enabled by default.
#
# Copy to a file ending in .rules (never .spocp or .bin), edit, and point
#   wallet_provider.attestation.assurance.rules_file
# at it. Validate with:  assurance-lint -rules <file>
#
# Format: advanced form, ONE RULE PER LINE, each rule preceded by a
# "# id: <name>" comment line. Ids are unique and appear in audit logs.
#
# Rules grant tiers by naming them: (tier (* set a b)) permits every listed
# tier, there is no implicit "at or below". There is no negation: deny is the
# absence of a rule. The floor level is always granted.
#
# Slot order is FIXED (schema version 1) because lists match by position:
#   (assure-ks (tier T)(evidence
#       (verified (fido2 (mds3)(aaguid)(uv)(cert))(platform (source)(app_id))(hsm (id)))
#       (claimed (plugin)(key_storage)(user_authentication)(certification))))
# Write a prefix of the slots; use the bare empty list, e.g. (platform), as
# "don't care". Only the (verified ...) group is backend-verified evidence;
# (claimed ...) is whatever the client said.
#
# THE AAGUID SET IS THE HARDWARE FILTER.  fido2_hw rests on one documented
# premise: an authenticator counts as hardware only if (a) its attestation is
# MDS3 trusted AND (b) the operator's rules list its AAGUID.  MDS3 trust alone
# does not say "hardware" (the backend does not read MDS3 keyProtection), so
# NO rule that grants a tier above the floor (key storage or user
# authentication) from verified fido2 evidence may omit an
# (aaguid (* set ...)) set.  assurance-lint warns on such a rule, and the
# shipped templates are tested to have no such finding.
#
# Replace the placeholder AAGUIDs (obviously not real: 00000000-...) with the
# authenticator models you have vetted as hardware and accept.

# The (aaguid (* set ...)) below is mandatory: it is the hardware filter.
# id: prod-fido2-mds3-ks
(assure-ks (tier (* set basic enhanced-basic moderate))(evidence (verified (fido2 (mds3 trusted)(aaguid (* set 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000002))))))

# User authentication at moderate needs proof of user verification (uv), which
# the backend does not record yet (planned follow-up). Until then every key
# resolves to the floor for user_authentication. Enable when (uv present) is
# emitted (uncomment the rule line and put a "# id: <name>" line before it):
#
#   (rule id would be: prod-fido2-mds3-ua; keep the aaguid set, it is the
#   hardware filter)
# (assure-ua (tier (* set basic enhanced-basic moderate))(evidence (verified (fido2 (mds3 trusted)(aaguid (* set 00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000001))(uv present)))))

# Wallet Instance Attestation (platform) rules belong to the follow-up that
# adds the assure-wia dimension; do not add them here yet.
